From ecac93c497e1dd789606566df7328f10062cab93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arealjim <6187715+arealjim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:13:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] steam-frame client: review 2026-10-21 close-out (M2-M12,
 L1-L9)

Patch 0016. Every Steam Frame client finding the adversarial review left OPEN or PARTLY,
closed as the smallest correct change; 734 unit checks (was 692), 0 failures.

M2  PollEvents: xrBeginSession/xrEndSession failures logged; a poll error is not "no events";
    session LOSS_PENDING and INSTANCE_LOSS_PENDING end the client with a clear line and exit
    status 3 (the client does not rebuild its session; the launcher restarts it).
M3  xrWaitSwapchainImage (and acquire) results checked: a failed eye is neither rendered nor
    released, and the layer is not submitted that frame.
M4  Reconnect, shaped like the sibling android-vr client and the server: discovery stays up
    through the connection; the server announces only while it has no client and drops one
    after 3 s without tracking, so an announce arriving while connected > 3 s means it
    restarted or forgot us. Also: the USB/TCP lost callback, and no video at all within
    FRAME_CLIENT_RECONNECT_S (default 5; 0 = off) of a connect. An idle server is left
    alone. Discovery runs on its own thread; the search gives up after 600 s. The direct
    (FRAME_CLIENT_SERVER) ask slows to every 5 s while connected.
M5  VideoDecoder::ResetStreamState: access unit, submit records, ready frames, pts history;
    called by OpenStream, ReconfigureStream and before every (re)connect wiring.
M6  avcodec_send_packet EAGAIN: drain the decoder's output, resend once; only a second
    refusal drops the access unit (counted, logged rate-limited).
M7  OpenStream refuses Codec::H264: the access-unit assembly reads HEVC NAL headers.
M8  PeekLatestPts names the frame TakeLatest would return (after the queue catch-up).
M9  lastConnect_ under connectMu_; the retry thread copies the current one per resend;
    testDropConnects_ atomic.
M10 Post-discovery wiring: a failed control socket, tracking connect or first ClientConnect
    stops the receiver and tracker before returning false; a failed decoder reconfigure
    with a nonzero size is a failed connect (the codec is closed); a zero size is said.
M11 runtime_paths.h: live-tuning files (frame-predict-ms, frame-passthrough,
    frame-stamp-lead-ms) read from $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR, else /dev/shm only when a regular
    file owned by this user; all debug dumps go to $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR as fresh 0600 files
    (O_EXCL | O_NOFOLLOW after an unlink), never through a planted symlink.
M12 g_poseEpoch: the velocity low-pass, the stamp-lead finite difference and the slip
    direction restart on every session state change, hidden/visible flip and reconnect.
L1  g_running is volatile sig_atomic_t.
L2  FindMemoryType UINT32_MAX checked at its three callers; frame fences and the readback
    dump's submit/wait checked; LoadFile checks tellg and the read.
L3  EnsureVideoTexture refuses a frame larger than the announced encode + 64 and a second
    re-creation within 1 s.
L4  serverName terminated before it is printed (discovery thread and connection).
L5  inet_ntop in PunchVideoPath; lastPunchNs_ atomic.
L6  latestMutex_ mutable; LastDecodeMs locks.
L7  The frame's own VIDEO_FLAG_ALPHA_BLEND rides SubmitNal -> FrameTiming; the layer flags,
    the blend mode and the shader's alpha key follow the displayed frame, not the latest
    received one.
L8  FRAME_CLIENT_PREDICT_MS / PREDICT_POS_MS clamped to 0..200, PREDICT_POS_TAU_MS to >= 0.
L9  xrGetDisplayRefreshRateFB's PFN is an App member.

Tests (tests/test_client_state.cpp): H.264 refused; the test clip decodes in stream mode
NAL by NAL; peek == take with and without a backlog; the alpha flag reaches FrameTiming;
reconfigure and reset forget the pending access unit and the ready frames and decoding
resumes with no old pts; runtime_paths reads the runtime dir, ignores symlinks, honours
only our own /dev/shm file, and a dump replaces a planted symlink with a 0600 regular file.

Also: CLIENT_CAPABILITY_PACING_LOCK set in ClientConnect (the Mac runtime gates its rate lock,
pacing_lock_wait_ms, on it since its own close-out). Defined here as 0x00002000: the Mac tree
chose 0x00000800, which on this branch is CLIENT_CAPABILITY_FOVEATION_CENTER (already sent, so
the Mac gate opens for this client either way); the Mac definition should move to 0x00002000.
